Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:19:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [M156] [maglev] Fix predecessor counting in the "smi case
 falls back to object case" logic
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Original change's description:
> [maglev] Fix predecessor counting in the "smi case falls back to object case" logic
>
> If the smi case "succeeds" but it just falls back to the object case
> which fails, that should not count as a success.
>
> Drive-by: Hardening; upgrading a DCHECK (which hits with one of the
> variants) to CHECK. Another variant was already hitting a CHECK.
>
> Fixed: 569286602
> Change-Id: Iae131e470629efd6a1c4c062512843944b6df138
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8518260
> Reviewed-by: Darius Mercadier <dmercadier@chromium.org>
> Commit-Queue: Marja Hölttä <marja@chromium.org>
> Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#110393}

(cherry picked from commit 6c626cef36527614a5f9001a2946ed4277118a77)

